 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The specialty directory answers the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. It lists every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. The directory lists specialties, not the full roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none. Every specialty appears on one page, with no paging. The directory is read-only, and a reader reaches it by its address alone. No navigation entry or link from another page leads to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on one page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding a specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is listed under it by full name, such as "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is listed under no specialty.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding several specialties is listed under each of them.
+2. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+3. Every specialty appears on the one page however many the clinic knows.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
